{"event_type":"review","id":"a67fa7dc5f0eef73383023d29ddcd3f1dec8b19e6d85d6c67b957937f425415c","occurred_at":"2026-11-16T23:15:43Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6a2594a1cf6100093603601031b1f1606b9d9ef52344a0b610de1feef5385602","sha256":"6a2594a1cf6100093603601031b1f1606b9d9ef52344a0b610de1feef5385602"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/73138015d4a175da0b866c2857a24a8cf5fd2f00fefb71a6c1347c16c09ceded","sha256":"73138015d4a175da0b866c2857a24a8cf5fd2f00fefb71a6c1347c16c09ceded"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f9101d586ee6fd4d5e063d5e426927d20f53183adadb0234a35394f22abb055d","sha256":"f9101d586ee6fd4d5e063d5e426927d20f53183adadb0234a35394f22abb055d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/de50958940c731d0c20390b4437104034ac85e5c64a7f817d73d8a3be09b58d2","sha256":"de50958940c731d0c20390b4437104034ac85e5c64a7f817d73d8a3be09b58d2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b2776b98934176033b77a032082998cd3d0e96fc0f022ed01392ab246a2d1708","sha256":"b2776b98934176033b77a032082998cd3d0e96fc0f022ed01392ab246a2d1708"}],"attempt_id":"113c9d6e22e02a0768c4a9e3702052a7ec3d2f7a00e2d2f87ad8c09b1b3dd19d:0:1","base":"1dd8793cb03a5945a04b77a941f2d4608bd703a7","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"8796beeffbed7fed986a94d3cfbf816f1242be29","body":"**Apply sibling keywords when a rule contains `oneOf`.**\n\n`schemaProblem` returns from its `oneOf` branch at `src/ops/crq/deploy/receiptValidation.ts:348`, so the type, `required`, and `properties` checks that follow it never run for that rule. A value that matches exactly one variant but violates a sibling constraint passes validation. If the local-review rule has this shape, `localReviewProblem` can reach `subscript(doc, 'identity')` at line 459 with a document that lacks `identity`. The sampling loop rethrows any error other than `OSError` at line 665, so one such document can abort the whole sample.\n\nReturn only when the variant count is wrong. Let the remaining keyword checks run otherwise:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   if (oneOf !== undefined) {\n     if (!Array.isArray(oneOf)) throw new PythonError('TypeError', 'oneOf is not a list');\n     const matches = oneOf.filter((branch) => schemaProblem(value, branch, at) === null).length;\n-    return matches === 1 ? null : `${where}: does not match exactly one variant`;\n+    if (matches !== 1) return `${where}: does not match exactly one variant`;\n   }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"d256fcb7db48129c75b77a75726041aaed7da2448035165422579a4696629348","intervals":[[348,348]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/receiptValidation.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Apply sibling keywords when a rule contains `oneOf`."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"810dd2c30e841a890b32460d8f9de5997f45dd1a","body":"**Recheck admission ownership before rollback effects.**\n\nAt `rollbackRecover.ts:369`, ownership is checked only before the asynchronous stop, drain and verification operations. Ownership can change during those operations, as the pre-switch recovery path explicitly recognizes at Line 317.\n\nIf ownership changes, Line 400 still switches checkout and Line 418 still starts triggers. Unlike `restoreBeforeSwitch`, rollback does not refuse the restart after ownership loss. Check current ownership immediately before checkout and again before restarting triggers. Route ownership loss to owner recovery.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 418-418","id":"f97394dec75918efe5b4a127972d2670d3690675226359c335e4f3c6ebd14d9e","intervals":[[400,400]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/rollbackRecover.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Recheck admission ownership before rollback effects."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b9146d2618c33d2038ba70e864f7607ddb2b34fd","body":"**Stop the tick-locked callback before the lock is released.**\n\n`withTickLock` rejects when `handle.lost` resolves, and its `finally` block then releases the lock. `fn()` keeps running. The `fn` parameter takes no cancellation signal, and `Promise.race` does not stop the pending work. The real binding can resolve `lost` while `fn()` is pending. `flockLockFs` resolves `lost` when the `flock(1)` holder exits while the lock is held and `release()` has not started. A holder that is killed or crashes can trigger this. After that, `switchCheckout` can continue its checkout, restore, and config-write steps without the lock, while another holder can acquire it.\n\nMake `lost` stop the work before the lock is released. Pass a cancellation signal to `fn` and to each effect it calls. Check that signal before every mutation. Keep the lock held until `fn()` settles, and reject only after it settles.","id":"da0b699e43abcd0a796690222606e0b2496e56fcbeb3b3bb65965b4005d0f04f","intervals":[[241,241]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/prepareHostEffects.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stop the tick-locked callback before the lock is released."}],"head":"72fe7672312b6b7e689157dccdc81e243c7c465a","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"493a90c1f2d838d0273a0429aedec69e28b1e0bc","intervals":[[1,619]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/artifactIdentity.ts"},{"blob":"d6acae711900d432d5d1dd7f310477add3b23e67","intervals":[[1,375]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/controllerRecords.ts"},{"blob":"3b198abc9c79fa3266dab396fc61045dc66117e6","intervals":[[1,424]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/deployOps.ts"},{"blob":"2560a8c8517cd109f1eb0d6868e286d91f22df9f","intervals":[[1,434]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/hostOverlay.ts"},{"blob":"b9146d2618c33d2038ba70e864f7607ddb2b34fd","intervals":[[1,597]],"path":"src/ops/crq/deploy/prepareHostEffects.ts"},{"blob